  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "The graph of $y=x^3$ is horizontally dilated by a factor of a third. What is the equivalent vertical dilation factor to give the same result?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$27$",
      "worked": "Replace $x$ by $\\dfrac{x}{\\frac{1}{3}}=3x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=(3x)^3\\\\y&=27x^3\\end{align*}$$\nThe equivalent vertical dilation factor is $27$.",
